title: Always rules are derived from kernel-signed rows; revoke deferred to a new event kind
summary: 'Standing always-allow rules are never stored: a RuleBook folds kernel-signed approval.request + approval.decide{always} + approval.rule.learned{repoKey} and matches (repoKey, tool, inputHash) exactly. inputHash is recomputed from the request row''s tool_input so no new digest lands in a normal row. Revoke needs approval.rule.revoked, which moves clientApiId, so it was not added. The ask-user answer note is checked against kernel-held questions before presence and logged only as noteHash; it is not inside the decisionSig preimage.'
